---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
// iOS is in review, so what this page may claim about iPhone and iPad is decided in ONE file that
// the landing page and the CanJam handout read too. When iOS is approved, flip IOS_STATUS there.
import { ATTUNE } from '../data/attune.js';

const email = 'jamey@warrenlabs.com';

// The FAQ, in ONE place: it renders the <details> below and the FAQPage node, so the visible
// answers and the structured data cannot drift. `a` is HTML; the schema text is `a` with the tags
// stripped. Only live-platform wording here (IOS_LIVE is true); if that ever flips back, the two
// platform answers need their review-state text again (see git history before 2026-11-11).
const faq: { q: string; a: string }[] = [
  {
    q: 'What is Attune?',
    a: `<p>Attune plays your music through a different tuning on the headphones you already own, and lets you flip back to the original instantly, at exactly the same loudness. You can aim at our house voice, at the tonal signature of another headphone, or at your own result from a blind listening test.</p>
<p>Everything is blind and loudness-matched, on your own music, so you're judging tone rather than volume.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What do I need to run it?',
    a: `<p><strong>macOS 12 or later on an Apple Silicon Mac</strong>, or <strong>iOS 16 or later</strong> on iPhone and iPad. A pair of headphones and some of your own music is all you need.</p>
<p>A demo track is bundled, so the whole flow works the moment you open it, before you load anything.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get started?',
    a: `<p>Choose <strong>your headphone</strong>, pick what to tune to under <strong>Tune to</strong>, then flip between <strong>Stock</strong> and <strong>Tuned</strong>. Same track, same loudness, only the tuning changes. When you're ready, use <strong>Find your sound</strong> to tune to your own taste.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work with Spotify or Apple Music?',
    a: `<p>Not inside Attune, and no app on macOS or iOS can. Streaming audio is protected end to end, so no third-party app is allowed to process it. Attune plays music you own: WAV, AIFF, FLAC, ALAC, AAC or MP3.</p>
<p>There is a way to get your tuning onto streaming, and it's the better answer anyway. With Attune Pro you can export your tuning as a standard AutoEq file and load it onto a DSP dongle at <a href="/tune/">warrenlabs.com/tune</a>. The dongle applies the EQ at the output, so it covers everything the device plays, streaming included, and it follows you to your phone. Loading needs a desktop copy of Chrome or Edge.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I use my own music?',
    a: `<p>Point Attune at your music folder or pick a single track. Attune only gets <strong>read-only</strong> access to the files you choose, and it remembers your folder so you don't have to re-pick it every launch.</p>
<p>Your music never leaves your device. See privacy, below.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Attune free? What does Pro add?',
    a: `<p>Free, permanently, and not a trial: tuning your headphone, every target, Find your sound, tone shaping, Fix by ear, the full parametric EQ for both ears together, importing your own measurements, and one saved sound kept for good. No account, no card.</p>
<p><strong>Attune Pro is a single purchase, $19.99 in the US</strong>, no subscription. It adds unlimited saved sounds; EQ export as a standard AutoEq file, so a tuning found here can travel to your phone, DAP or dongle, with your tone and EQ bands included; and separate left and right EQ bands. It's a Universal Purchase, so buying it on the Mac unlocks it on iPhone and iPad, and the other way round.</p>
<p><strong>Importing your own measurement is free and will not become a paid feature.</strong></p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "Whose measurements are these? My headphone isn't listed.",
    a: `<p>Ours. Every headphone in Attune was measured here on a miniDSP EARS Pro. Nothing is pulled from a public database. We'd rather ship a handful we can stand behind than thousands we can't, and the corpus grows as we measure.</p>
<p>If yours isn't there, choose <strong>Mine isn't here</strong>. You can <strong>shape the tone by ear</strong> (Warmer, Brighter, Less sharp, and Fix by ear); this changes the tone but cannot correct the headphone, because we have no measurement of it. You can also <strong>import your own measurement</strong> in CSV, AutoEq or squig format and Attune will voice-match to it exactly as it would to a bundled one: we take the difference between the two and correct for it, loudness-matched. That path is free. Or press <strong>Request this headphone</strong> to tell us what to measure next, or <strong>send us the headphone</strong>: we measure it on our rig, publish the result either way, and add it.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there an iPhone version?',
    a: `<p>Yes. Attune is on iPhone and iPad, and Attune Pro is a Universal Purchase, so one unlock covers Mac and iOS in either direction.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is the graph empty when I open it?',
    a: `<p>Because no headphone is chosen yet, and that's deliberate. The correction is computed from a real measured response, so until Attune knows which headphones you own there's nothing honest to draw. Choose yours under <strong>Your headphone</strong>, or pick <strong>Mine isn't here</strong> to shape the tone by ear. The graph and the Stock and Tuned comparison come alive immediately.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does Tuned sound quieter?',
    a: `<p>It doesn't. Both sides are set to the same loudness on purpose, and we measured the residual rather than assuming it: 0.04 to 1.0 dB across the headphones we tested.</p>
<p>That matching is the whole point of the comparison. Anything even slightly louder sounds better for the first few seconds, every time, to everyone. Without level matching you aren't comparing tunings, you're just finding out which one is louder. If Tuned feels quieter, what you're hearing is usually a bass or treble shift, not a level shift.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work with wireless or Bluetooth headphones?',
    a: `<p>It will play through them, and you can tune them, but wired is the honest recommendation. Bluetooth headphones usually apply their own processing that we can't see or account for, so what you'd be correcting is the headphone plus whatever its firmware is already doing. Our measurements are of the headphone.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What about my privacy?',
    a: `<p>Attune has <strong>no account and no sign-in</strong>. Your music, your listening and your tunings stay on your device. It contacts our server only if you press <strong>Request this headphone</strong>, and then it sends just the name you typed, the app version and your platform.</p>
<p>Full details on our <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "The app won't open, or I can't hear a difference.",
    a: `<p><strong>Won't open:</strong> confirm you're on macOS 12 or later with Apple Silicon, or iOS 16 or later, and that Attune came from the App Store. Quit and relaunch. If it still won't start, email us your OS version and device model.</p>
<p><strong>No difference:</strong> check that a headphone is selected, that the correct <strong>output device</strong> is chosen inside Attune, and that a track is playing. Then remember the Stock and Tuned comparison is <strong>loudness-matched on purpose</strong>. Listen for a change in <em>tone</em>, not a jump in level. Some pairs and some targets are a small correction, and a small correction is a small difference.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: "What's the demo track?",
    a: `<p>"Off Road", written and performed by Jamey Warren and Kevin Toll, © 2021. Jamey is a rights holder, which is why it can ship with the app.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do refunds work?',
    a: `<p>Anything bought through the App Store is handled by Apple. Visit <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a> to request a refund.</p>`,
  },
];

const plain = (html: string) => html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').replace(/ ([.,;:)])/g, '$1').trim();

const faqPage = {
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map(({ q, a }) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: plain(a) },
  })),
};
---

<Layout
  title="Support · Warren Labs"
  description={`Help and support for Attune, the headphone voice-matching and preference-tuning app for ${ATTUNE.metaPlatforms}. FAQ, troubleshooting, and how to reach a real person.`}
  jsonLd={faqPage}
>
  <Nav variant="home" />
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Support</span>
      <h1 class="as-h2">We're here to help.</h1>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Answers to the most common questions are below. If you don't find what you need,
        email us directly. A real person reads every message.
      </p>

      <p class="contact">
        <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Attune%20support`}>{email}</a><span class="muted">. We usually reply within two business days.</span>
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked</h3>

      {
        faq.map(({ q, a }) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{q}</summary>
            <div class="answer" set:html={a} />
          </details>
        ))
      }

      <h3>Reporting a bug</h3>
      <p>The more of this you can include, the faster we can help:</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Your <strong>OS version</strong>: Apple menu → About This Mac, or Settings → General → About</li>
        <li>Your <strong>device</strong>: e.g. MacBook Air (M2, 2022), or iPhone 15 Pro</li>
        <li><strong>What you did</strong>: the steps that led to the problem</li>
        <li><strong>What you expected</strong> vs. <strong>what happened</strong></li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it's something you can see</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Footer variant="home" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h3 { margin: 36px 0 10px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.65; }

  .contact { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .contact .muted { opacity: 0.55; font-size: 0.92rem; }

  .checklist { margin: 6px 0 14px; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .checklist li { margin: 0 0 4px; }

  details {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    padding: 13px 0;
  }
  details:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: '+'; opacity: 0.55; }
  details[open] summary::after { content: '–'; }
  .answer { margin-top: 10px; opacity: 0.82; }
  /* :global because the answers arrive through set:html, which carries no scope attribute. */
  .answer :global(p) { margin: 0 0 10px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .answer :global(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
